-- A loan is open while it has no return, and late once its due date is past. A member has an
-- open loan, or a late loan, when one of its loans is. Nothing assigns `dueOn`, so time passing
-- can only make a loan late, never not late. A new Return only adds to its loan's `returns`, so
-- it can only take a loan out of `count(returns) < 1`, never put one in. Rule NoticeMembers runs
-- for a member with an open loan and no notice.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", these lines among others. Each is followed in the report by its "In the spec:"
-- lines, left out here.
--
--   ### Loan
--   - A new Return can now make a Loan stop being an OpenLoan.
--   - Time passing can now make a Loan become a LateLoan.
--   ### Member
--   - Time passing can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateLoan.
--   - Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithLateLoan.
--   - A new Return can now make a Member become a MemberWithOpenLoan.
--   - A new Return can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithOpenLoan.
--   ### Return
--   - A new Return can now cause NoticeMembers to run, later rather than in the same commit.
--
-- On one loan the direction is right: OpenLoan and LateLoan each get one line. Read through
-- `exists (loans where ...)`, the same two conditions get both directions, and three lines
-- cannot happen: "Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithLateLoan", "A new
-- Return can now make a Member become a MemberWithOpenLoan", and "A new Return can now cause
-- NoticeMembers to run". No refinement is named inside a condition and no sum is read, so this
-- is not the case in `33-positive-payment-enters-overdue-accepted.velle` (OQ182). The report's
-- line "NoticeMembers can now cause NoticeMembers to run" is the case in
-- `36-compare-rule-runs-itself-accepted.velle`.
act Member { name: text }

act Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

act Return { loan: one Loan }

shape Notice { member: one Member }

shape OpenLoan = Loan where count(returns) < 1

shape LateLoan = Loan where dueOn < today

shape MemberWithLateLoan = Member where exists (loans where dueOn < today)

shape MemberWithOpenLoan = Member where exists (loans where count(returns) < 1)

rule NoticeMembers when (Member where exists (loans where count(returns) < 1) and not exists Notice for this) on Nightly {
    Notice from { member: this }
}
